## 2. How the integration works


### Full lifecycle (ASCII diagram)


```
                ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
                │ 1. INITIAL CHECKOUT (browser redirect flow)  │
                ├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
user clicks ──▶│ our backend builds an HTML form with:        │
"Upgrade"       │   • orderId (unique, encodes profile id)     │
                │   • orderAmount, currency, payerEmail        │
                │   • extRecurringfrequency = 30 (or 365)      │
                │   • extRecurringenddate = today + 1825 days  │
                │   • extTokenOptions = '100' (request token)  │
                │   • confirmUrl / cancelUrl                   │
                │   • digest (SHA256 of canonical field order  │
                │     + sharedSecret)                          │
                └─────────────┬────────────────────────────────┘
                              │ user submits form
                              ▼
                ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
                │ Cardlink hosts payment page (card entry +    │
                │ 3DSv2 challenge if required)                 │
                └─────────────┬────────────────────────────────┘
                              │
           ┌──────────────────┴──────────────────┐
           │                                     │
           ▼  Success (CAPTURED / AUTHORIZED)    ▼  Failure (REFUSED / ERROR)
Cardlink POSTs to confirmUrl                Cardlink POSTs to cancelUrl
with the payment result + extToken          (or same confirmUrl with status)
(our subscription becomes active            and the user is redirected back.
in DB; we store the token)
                              │
                              ▼
       ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
       │ 2. SCHEDULED RECURRING — Cardlink fires every N days    │
       │    (every 30 days for monthly, 365 for yearly).         │
       │    Same-day automatic retries at 07:00 / 15:00 / 23:00  │
       │    Athens time on failure.                              │
       │    Each child fired gets orderId = "{masterOrderId}/N"  │
       │    where N = Sequence (2, 3, 4, …).                     │
       └─────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────┘
                     │ Cardlink POSTs notification to the
                     │ "Recurring notify URL" configured in
                     │ THEIR merchant portal (NOT to confirmUrl).
                     ▼
       ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
       │ Our webhook updates the subscription row + records the  │
       │ attempt in the history table.                           │
       └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘


                     Parallel safety net:
       ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
       │ 3. CRON — daily 06:00 UTC, our own /api/cron/worldline- │
       │    renewals. Finds subscriptions with:                  │
       │      a) status=active AND currentPeriodEnd <= tomorrow  │
       │         → "renewal due" — fire SaleRequest via XML      │
       │      b) status=past_due AND last attempt >= 3d ago      │
       │         → "retry" (up to MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS=3)          │
       │    Marks subscription canceled after retries exhausted. │
       └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```


### Why we have BOTH Cardlink-scheduled recurring AND our own cron


Because Cardlink's "Recurring notify URL" is configured per-merchant in their **portal**, not via API. If it's not configured, Cardlink will still charge the card on schedule but **we'll never know**. Our cron is a safety net that catches stale `currentPeriodEnd` rows and triggers a charge ourselves.


> **⚠️ Important:** if the notify URL **is** configured AND the cron is also active, you risk **double-charging** — Cardlink charges at 07:00 Athens, our cron charges at 09:00 Athens (06:00 UTC), both succeed. Set the portal URL FIRST, then let the cron be the safety net.


---


## 3. Critical Cardlink portal config


**This cannot be set via API. It must be done by the merchant in Cardlink's MPI/VPOS/FSS Manager backend:**


| Field | Value | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **Recurring notify URL** | `https://<your-domain>/api/webhooks/worldline` (or Django equivalent) | Where Cardlink POSTs each recurring-child notification. Empty here = silent charges, our DB never updates. |
| **Webhooks** (alternative section, up to 5 URLs) | Same URL | Newer mechanism. Either field works; both can be set. |


If you skip this, the entire history feature fills only with cron-initiated entries (because that's the only code path that knows about charges).


