## 6. Data model


### Table: `subscriptions`


> All amounts in **cents** as `INTEGER`. All timestamps in UTC, stored as `TIMESTAMP(3) WITHOUT TIME ZONE` (Postgres). Render in Athens at presentation time.


| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | TEXT PK | cuid |
| `pid` | TEXT UNIQUE FK → profiles | one subscription per profile |
| `provider` | enum (`stripe`, `worldline`, `paypal`, `eurobank`, `manual`) | multi-provider hooks |
| `providerCustomerId` | TEXT UNIQUE NULL | for Worldline = the MID |
| `providerSubscriptionId` | TEXT UNIQUE NULL | for Worldline = the initial orderId |
| `worldlineToken` | TEXT NULL | stored card token (Cardlink's `extToken`) |
| `worldlineTokenExp` | TEXT NULL | format YYYYMMDD |
| `worldlineMasterOrderId` | TEXT NULL | original master orderId — used to match recurring children |
| `plan` | enum (`free`, `promoted`) | |
| `status` | enum (`active`, `past_due`, `canceled`, `incomplete`, `trialing`, `unpaid`) | |
| `billingInterval` | enum (`month`, `year`) NULL | |
| `currentPeriodStart` | TIMESTAMP NULL | |
| `currentPeriodEnd` | TIMESTAMP NULL | **next-charge anchor**; computed as `previous_end + 30 days` |
| `cancelAtPeriodEnd` | BOOLEAN DEFAULT false | |
| `canceledAt` | TIMESTAMP NULL | |
| `amount` | INT NULL | current price in cents |
| `currency` | TEXT DEFAULT 'eur' | |
| `paymentMethodType` / `Last4` / `Brand` | TEXT NULL | |
| `firstPaymentAt`, `lastPaymentAt` | TIMESTAMP NULL | analytics |
| `paymentCount` | INT DEFAULT 0 | analytics |
| `totalPaidLifetime` | INT DEFAULT 0 | cents accumulated |
| `discountCode`, `discountPercentOff`, `discountAmountOff` | NULL | optional coupon |
| `billing` | JSON NULL | snapshot of invoice / receipt prefs at checkout |
| `createdAt`, `updatedAt` | TIMESTAMP | |


### Table: `subscription_payment_attempts` (history)


```sql
CREATE TYPE "PaymentAttemptStatus" AS ENUM (
 'CAPTURED', 'AUTHORIZED', 'REFUSED', 'REFUSEDRISK', 'CANCELED', 'ERROR'
);
CREATE TYPE "PaymentAttemptSource" AS ENUM (
 'initial', 'recurring_child', 'cron_renewal', 'cron_retry', 'manual'
);


CREATE TABLE "subscription_payment_attempts" (
 "id"             TEXT NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY,
 "subscriptionId" TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES "subscriptions"("id") ON DELETE CASCADE,
 "status"         "PaymentAttemptStatus" NOT NULL,
 "source"         "PaymentAttemptSource" NOT NULL,
 "amount"         INTEGER NOT NULL,          -- cents
 "currency"       TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'eur',
 "sequence"       INTEGER,                   -- Cardlink Sequence (1, 2, 3, …)
 "txId"           TEXT,                      -- Cardlink TX ID
 "paymentRef"     TEXT,                      -- Cardlink payment reference
 "orderId"        TEXT,                      -- full Cardlink orderId, e.g. DOLxxx/3
 "message"        TEXT,                      -- gateway response message
 "errorMessage"   TEXT,                      -- technical exception detail
 "createdAt"      TIMESTAMP(3) NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);


CREATE INDEX ON subscription_payment_attempts (subscriptionId, createdAt);
CREATE INDEX ON subscription_payment_attempts (status, createdAt);
CREATE INDEX ON subscription_payment_attempts (txId);
```


### Status enum meanings (match Cardlink's response values exactly)


| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `CAPTURED` | Charged + committed to settlement |
| `AUTHORIZED` | Authorized only, capture pending (rare with Cardlink) |
| `REFUSED` | Card declined (insufficient funds, expired, etc.) |
| `REFUSEDRISK` | Rejected by Cardlink's fraud / risk engine |
| `CANCELED` | User canceled at the hosted payment page (only for `initial`) |
| `ERROR` | Network / technical error |


### Source enum meanings


| Source | When |
|---|---|
| `initial` | User-initiated first checkout. Sequence = 1. |
| `recurring_child` | Cardlink's scheduled-recurring webhook (Sequence ≥ 2). |
| `cron_renewal` | Our daily cron sent an XML SaleRequest for a `currentPeriodEnd <= tomorrow` subscription. |
| `cron_retry` | Our cron retrying a `past_due` subscription. |
| `manual` | Admin or backfill insert. |


### Why TWO enums (`status` AND `source`)
- `status` answers **what happened** to this attempt (success / failure type).
- `source` answers **who triggered** it (user checkout, Cardlink auto-charge, our cron).


Same status (e.g. `CAPTURED`) can come from different sources. Without `source`, you cannot tell a Cardlink-initiated successful charge apart from a cron-initiated one — which matters for debugging double-charges and verifying the notify-URL config.


