## 7. SQL migrations (run manually on Supabase SQL Editor)


> ⚠️ **DO NOT auto-run.** Copy each block manually into Supabase → SQL Editor and inspect before pressing Run. Order matters: migration first, then deploy code, then (optionally) backfill.


### 7.1 Migration — create the history table


Safe to run on production. Adds new enums/table/indexes/FK only. Does **not** touch any existing data or column.


```sql
-- Enums ---------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE TYPE "PaymentAttemptStatus" AS ENUM (
 'CAPTURED', 'AUTHORIZED', 'REFUSED', 'REFUSEDRISK', 'CANCELED', 'ERROR'
);


CREATE TYPE "PaymentAttemptSource" AS ENUM (
 'initial', 'recurring_child', 'cron_renewal', 'cron_retry', 'manual'
);


-- Table ---------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE TABLE "subscription_payment_attempts" (
 "id"             TEXT                    NOT NULL,
 "subscriptionId" TEXT                    NOT NULL,
 "status"         "PaymentAttemptStatus"  NOT NULL,
 "source"         "PaymentAttemptSource"  NOT NULL,
 "amount"         INTEGER                 NOT NULL,
 "currency"       TEXT                    NOT NULL DEFAULT 'eur',
 "sequence"       INTEGER,
 "txId"           TEXT,
 "paymentRef"     TEXT,
 "orderId"        TEXT,
 "message"        TEXT,
 "errorMessage"   TEXT,
 "createdAt"      TIMESTAMP(3)            NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
 CONSTRAINT "subscription_payment_attempts_pkey" PRIMARY KEY ("id")
);


-- Indexes -------------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE INDEX "subscription_payment_attempts_subscriptionId_createdAt_idx"
 ON "subscription_payment_attempts" ("subscriptionId", "createdAt");
CREATE INDEX "subscription_payment_attempts_status_createdAt_idx"
 ON "subscription_payment_attempts" ("status", "createdAt");
CREATE INDEX "subscription_payment_attempts_txId_idx"
 ON "subscription_payment_attempts" ("txId");


-- Foreign key ---------------------------------------------------------------
ALTER TABLE "subscription_payment_attempts"
 ADD CONSTRAINT "subscription_payment_attempts_subscriptionId_fkey"
 FOREIGN KEY ("subscriptionId")
 REFERENCES "subscriptions" ("id")
 ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE;
```


### 7.2 Verification


```sql
SELECT typname FROM pg_type
WHERE typname IN ('PaymentAttemptStatus', 'PaymentAttemptSource');
-- expect 2 rows


SELECT COUNT(*) FROM "subscription_payment_attempts";
-- expect 0
```


### 7.3 Backfill (optional) — the test account history


Idempotent: re-running is safe (uses `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` on the primary key).


