## 8. Required environment variables


| Var | Where | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `PAYMENTS_TEST_MODE` | runtime | `true` (sandbox) / `false` (live) |
| `WORLDLINE_TEST_MID` | sandbox MID | `0025368903` |
| `WORLDLINE_TEST_SHARED_SECRET` | sandbox HMAC secret | (32+ chars) |
| `WORLDLINE_LIVE_MID` | production MID | (assigned by acquirer) |
| `WORLDLINE_LIVE_SHARED_SECRET` | production HMAC secret | (32+ chars) |
| `CRON_SECRET` | bearer token gating `/api/cron/*` | random 32+ chars |
| `BETTER_AUTH_URL` (Next-specific) / `SITE_URL` (Django) | absolute origin used to build `confirmUrl` / `cancelUrl` | `https://doulitsa.gr` |
| `TZ` | runtime timezone (where settable — **NOT on Vercel Dashboard, reserved**) | `Europe/Athens` |


### Cardlink endpoints


| Environment | Redirect URL | XML URL |
|---|---|---|
| Sandbox | `https://eurocommerce-test.cardlink.gr/vpos/shophandlermpi` | `https://eurocommerce-test.cardlink.gr/vpos/xmlpayvpos` |
| Production | `https://vpos.eurocommerce.gr/vpos/shophandlermpi` | `https://vpos.eurocommerce.gr/vpos/xmlpayvpos` |


---


## 9. Digest algorithms


### 9.1 Redirect form digest (initial checkout)


Fixed 46-field canonical order, concatenated as strings (no separator), then SHA-256 over UTF-8, then Base64-encoded. Empty fields = empty string (still concatenated in position).


Field order (this matters — verified empirically against Cardlink sandbox):


```
version, mid, lang, deviceCategory, orderid, orderDesc,
orderAmount, currency, payerEmail, payerPhone, billCountry,
billState, billZip, billCity, billAddress, weight, dimensions,
shipCountry, shipState, shipZip, shipCity, shipAddress,
addFraudScore, maxPayRetries, reject3dsU, payMethod, trType,
extInstallmentoffset, extInstallmentperiod, extRecurringfrequency,
extRecurringenddate, blockScore, cssUrl, confirmUrl, cancelUrl,
extTokenOptions, extToken,
var1, var2, var3, var4, var5, var6, var7, var8, var9
```


**Then append the sharedSecret BEFORE hashing:**


```
digest = base64( sha256( utf8( concat(field_values) + sharedSecret ) ) )
```


For incoming response digest validation, iterate `formData` in POST insertion order, skip the `digest` field itself, concat all values, append sharedSecret, hash, compare. (Don't rely on a fixed field order for incoming — Cardlink sends whatever they want and order matters.)


### 9.2 XML API digest (SaleRequest / RecurringOperationRequest)


Different algorithm from the redirect form digest:


```
digest = base64( sha256( utf8( canonicalized_message_xml + sharedSecret ) ) )
```


The `canonicalized_message_xml` is the `<Message>...</Message>` element with namespaces ON the Message tag in canonical order. See `src/lib/payment/providers/worldline/xml.ts` `cancelRecurring` for the exact byte-pattern (we had to build the XML manually — fast-xml-parser produced equivalent-but-not-byte-identical output that failed verification).


Cardlink also wants timestamps in ISO 8601 with offset (e.g. `2026-05-16T11:23:00.000+03:00`), **not** UTC `Z` suffix.


